    "summary": "First‑ever Corinna debut, strong Space, but mix issues hinder listening",
    "blurb": "The show opens with the debut of Corinna and delivers a fiery Space featuring the Ollin Arageed theme. Jerry shines on Not Fade Away and the second‑set jam, though the matrix mix buries some instruments. Overall performance is solid but recording quality varies.",
    "review": "Feb 23 1992 at the Oakland‑Alameda County Coliseum captures a night of mixed fortunes for the Dead. The setlist kicks off with the historic first performance of Corinna, a bright moment that immediately sets an upbeat tone. Highlights roll forward into the second set where China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segues into a marathon Playing In The Band > Terrapin Station → Drums → Space sequence; the Space here is singled out for its “Ollin Arageed” theme and Jerry’s “very Dead” guitar work, earning high praise from the soundboard capture. Not Fade Away closes the set with Jerry’s lead guitar cutting through, giving fans a classic finish, followed by a soulful Box of Rain encore.\n\nHowever, the listening experience is uneven. The matrix recording suffers from an echo‑y, thin mix that often drowns out Jerry and Phil, especially on Terrapin Station and later in the set, while the drum/space segment feels over‑extended to some ears. Audience recordings are noisy and lack clarity, and one reviewer even called the first‑time song at the end a misstep that ruined the flow. The best‑sounding source is the high‑quality soundboard capture (gd1992-02-23.set2.sbd.walker-scotton.miller), which presents the band in clear balance and lets Jerry’s top‑form playing shine through.",
